{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8puaqXCjeCiieypVvFN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `wt-select-files` goes through the diff, and applied selections are forgotten from the torrent's close handler (source scan)\n\nThe engine now sends webtorrent only the file selections that changed, so sending the same list twice does nothing. The full `npm test` run passes (4400 tests, lint included). It's in two commits on the branch.\n\n**The diff:** the new `src/engine/selections.js` exports `diffSelections(applied, requested)`. It returns which files to select, which to deselect, and whether webtorrent's default whole-torrent selection still has to be removed. When there are no earlier selections for a torrent, it does what the old code did on every call: remove the default, select every wanted file and deselect the rest. After that, it only reports files whose state flipped. `test/unit/engine-selections.js` tests it with plain values and covers the first three checklist items.\n\n**The wiring:** `src/engine/index.js` keeps a per-torrent map of the selections last applied, called `appliedSelections`. `selectFiles` diffs against that map, applies only the changes and stores what it applied. The entry is deleted in `torrentClose`, after the check that skips cleanup when a duplicate add closes, so a resumed torrent starts from the default selection again. Two new source-scan tests in `test/unit/engine-torrent-close-wiring.js` check both parts.\n\nOne change to my own new test while getting it green: the scan regex didn't allow a line break inside the `diffSelections(` call, and the code has one. I loosened only the whitespace match; the assertion checks the same thing.\n\nI added a `selections.js` section to `src/engine/AGENTS.md` and listed the map in its close-handler section. Notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` and not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":67383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"output_tokens":571,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f96e20b8-4586-4652-a1ec-e1f2211c71ab","uuid":"49974f2f-f5df-4824-a1ec-d312746124a0","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:22:23.381Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8puaadgt7cLrtG8bfAW"}
